---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Healthcare AI Consulting"
	description="AI solutions for healthcare and regulated industries — patient access, care coordination, AI governance, and open standards. Built on two decades of healthcare technology leadership."
>
	<Nav />

	<!-- Hero -->
	<section class="hero">
		<p class="hero-eyebrow">Healthcare AI · Regulated Industries</p>
		<h1>AI for healthcare, governed from the start.</h1>
		<p class="hero-subhead">
			Ohana Consulting delivers AI solutions across patient access, care coordination, and clinical engagement —
			and the governance infrastructure to ensure they're compliant, auditable, and trusted by the clinicians and patients who depend on them.
		</p>
		<div class="hero-ctas">
			<a href="/services" class="btn btn-primary">Our Services</a>
			<a href="/contact" class="btn btn-secondary">Start a Conversation</a>
		</div>
	</section>

	<hr class="section-divider" />

	<!-- What we do -->
	<section class="section">
		<p class="section-label">What we do</p>
		<h2>Where healthcare meets AI governance.</h2>
		<p class="section-intro">
			Deploying AI in a regulated environment is not the same problem as deploying AI. The clinical workflow, the
			interoperability requirements, the compliance obligations, and the ethical accountability don't go away
			because a model is involved — they get harder. We've been living inside these problems for twenty years.
		</p>
		<div class="service-grid">
			<div class="service-card">
				<h3>AI Governance & Compliance</h3>
				<p>
					Governance that spans the development cycle and runtime — not a checkbox exercise. Structured context methodology
					to ensure AI systems in clinical settings are auditable, fair, and aligned with CHAI, HIPAA, and NIST AI RMF.
				</p>
				<a href="/services#governance" class="service-card-link">Learn more &rarr;</a>
			</div>
			<div class="service-card">
				<h3>Care Coordination & Patient Engagement</h3>
				<p>
					Chronic condition management, care plan adherence, and multi-provider coordination powered by AI —
					built on FHIR and SMART on FHIR so the data moves with the patient, not the institution.
				</p>
				<a href="/services#care-coordination" class="service-card-link">Learn more &rarr;</a>
			</div>
			<div class="service-card">
				<h3>Patient Access to Care</h3>
				<p>
					AI-driven triage, appointment optimization, and prior authorization guidance that reduces friction for
					patients and administrative burden for staff — while staying inside payer and regulatory guardrails.
				</p>
				<a href="/services#patient-access" class="service-card-link">Learn more &rarr;</a>
			</div>
			<div class="service-card">
				<h3>Open Standards & Interoperability</h3>
				<p>
					FHIR, SMART, NCPDP SCRIPT, HL7, and 21st Century Cures compliance aren't obstacles — they're the
					foundation. We design integrations that work across EHRs and payer systems without proprietary lock-in.
				</p>
				<a href="/services#standards" class="service-card-link">Learn more &rarr;</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<hr class="section-divider" />

	<!-- Credibility section -->
	<section class="section">
		<p class="section-label">Experience</p>
		<h2>The background that earns the opinion.</h2>
		<p class="section-intro">
			The case for AI in healthcare is not new. Neither are the reasons it fails — misalignment with clinical workflow,
			inadequate governance, and standards that were designed for human readers rather than AI systems.
			Understanding all three layers at once is rare. It's what Ohana brings.
		</p>
		<ul class="highlight-list">
			<li>
				<strong>Optum / UnitedHealth Group — 8 years</strong>
				Technology executive for advanced clinical solutions. Designed and built Calypso, an internal integration platform
				for multi-EHR FHIR data exchange using SMART on FHIR — one application, any EHR. Led Optum's technical engagement
				on 21st Century Cures. Contributed to AI-driven clinical decision support and prior authorization guidance.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Red Hat</strong>
				Architect and designer for embedded systems, OpenStack, and OpenShift (Docker/Kubernetes). Deep foundation in
				cloud-native infrastructure — the same stack that now runs AI workloads in production.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>IBM — Software Development Product Management</strong>
				Managed the full IBM software portfolio. Conceived and drove the open sourcing of Eclipse — one of the most
				consequential decisions in enterprise open source. Built deep expertise in open standards and their strategic use
				in commercial offerings.
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p style="margin-top: 2rem;">
			<a href="/about" class="btn btn-secondary">Full background &rarr;</a>
		</p>
	</section>

	<hr class="section-divider" />

	<!-- Governance callout -->
	<section class="section">
		<p class="section-label">The governance problem</p>
		<h2>Standards written for humans don't govern AI systems.</h2>
		<p class="section-intro">
			CHAI, HIPAA, NIST AI RMF, and clinical ethics frameworks are written in natural language for human reviewers.
			AI systems operate on structured data and explicit constraints. The gap between them is where compliance breaks down —
			and where patient safety risk accumulates.
		</p>
		<p class="section-intro">
			Ohana's approach to AI governance in regulated environments uses structured context methodology to bridge that gap:
			governance requirements travel from the standards body to the AI agent, intact and machine-readable.
			The result is auditability that doesn't require manual review of every inference.
		</p>
		<p>
			<a href="https://structuredcontext.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-secondary">
				Structured Context specification &rarr;
			</a>
		</p>
	</section>

	<!-- CTA banner -->
	<div class="cta-banner">
		<div class="cta-banner-inner">
			<div>
				<h2>Ready to talk through your use case?</h2>
				<p>Whether it's a specific deployment challenge, a governance architecture question, or a standards integration — we'll engage directly with the problem.</p>
			</div>
			<a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Get in Touch</a>
		</div>
	</div>

	<SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
